    "id": "leaving-circuit",
    "title": "Leaving the circuit and the frequency",
    "shortExplanation": "Report where you leave the circuit, then tell the station before you change frequency.",
    "overview": [
      "Report leaving the circuit with the exit point and your altitude, so arriving traffic knows where you are.",
      "Before you change frequency, tell the station where you go. Around Piła, FIS is split by a line through the airfield: Gdańsk Information to the north, Poznań Information to the south."
    ],
    "whyItMatters": "A station that does not know you left may start a search when you stop answering.",
    "references": [
      {
        "source": "ICAO Doc 9432 Manual of Radiotelephony",
        "section": "2.8.2 Transfer of communications"
      },
